.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt B2I_PVK_BIO_EX 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm b2i_PVK_bio ,
.Nm b2i_PVK_bio_ex ,
.Nm i2b_PVK_bio ,
.Nm i2b_PVK_bio_ex
.Nd Decode and encode functions for reading and writing MSBLOB format private keys
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/pem.h
.Ft EVP_PKEY *
.Fo b2i_PVK_bio
.Fa "BIO *in"
.Fa "pem_password_cb *cb"
.Fa "void *u"
.Fc
.Ft EVP_PKEY *
.Fo b2i_PVK_bio_ex
.Fa "BIO *in"
.Fa "pem_password_cb *cb"
.Fa "void *u"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo i2b_PVK_bio
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fa "const EVP_PKEY *pk"
.Fa "int enclevel"
.Fa "pem_password_cb *cb"
.Fa "void *u"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo i2b_PVK_bio_ex
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fa "const EVP_PKEY *pk"
.Fa "int enclevel"
.Fa "pem_password_cb *cb"
.Fa "void *u"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn b2i_PVK_bio_ex
decodes a private key of MSBLOB format read from a
.Vt BIO .
It attempts to automatically determine the key type.
If the key is encrypted then
.Fa cb
is called with the user data
.Fa u
in order to obtain a password to decrypt the key.
The supplied library context
.Fa libctx
and property query string
.Fa propq
are used in any decrypt operation.
.Pp
.Fn b2i_PVK_bio
does the same as
.Fn b2i_PVK_bio_ex
except that the default library context and property query string are
used.
.Pp
.Fn i2b_PVK_bio_ex
encodes
.Fa pk
using MSBLOB format.
If
.Fa enclevel
is 1 then a password obtained via
.Vt pem_password_cb
is used to encrypt the private key.
If
.Fa enclevel
is 0 then no encryption is applied.
The user data in
.Fa u
is passed to the password callback.
The supplied library context
.Fa libctx
and property query string
.Fa propq
are used in any decrypt operation.
.Pp
.Fn i2b_PVK_bio
does the same as
.Fn i2b_PVK_bio_ex
except that the default library context and property query string are
used.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn b2i_PVK_bio
and
.Fn b2i_PVK_bio_ex
functions return a valid
.Sy EVP_KEY
structure or
.Dv NULL
if an error occurs.
The error code can be obtained by calling
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
.Pp
.Fn i2b_PVK_bio
and
.Fn i2b_PVK_bio_ex
return the number of bytes successfully encoded or a negative value if
an error occurs.
The error code can be obtained by calling
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr crypto 7 ,
.Xr d2i_PKCS8PrivateKey_bio 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn b2i_PVK_bio_ex
and
.Fn i2b_PVK_bio_ex
were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
